  "term": "assonance",
  "definition": "In historical psychiatric writing, assonance refers to a pattern of thought in which ideas are linked mainly by similarity of sound between words rather than by meaning. One word prompts another that sounds like it, and this can contribute to apparently incoherent speech.",
